Offer Thai in the ASR language list

`CUSTOM_ASR_DEFAULT_LANGUAGES` is what a custom OpenAI-compatible speech provider
offers in its language menu. It carries `zh`, `en`, `ja`, `ko`, `es`, `fr`, `de`,
`ru`, `ar`, `pt`, `it` and `hi` — and no `th`, so Thai cannot be chosen at all.

The default is `zh` (`lib/store/settings.ts:482`) and it is sent with the request
(`lib/audio/asr-providers.ts:235`), so Whisper is told the audio is Chinese and
obliges. Thai speech comes back as Chinese text: a Thai sentence transcribed as
`我愛你`. That reads like a broken model and is the API doing exactly as asked.

Nothing else was missing. `settings.lang_th` is already "ไทย" in all thirteen
locale files, so the label has been waiting for an option to attach to — what is
absent is an entry in an array, which is data, and no locale file can add one.

Whisper supports Thai, and this list is the set of choices offered rather than a
claim about a particular model: a provider that cannot handle a language declares
its own `supportedLanguages`, the way `funasr` does with
`['auto','zh','en','ja','ko','yue']`. That entry is deliberately left alone —
SenseVoice really cannot do Thai, and adding it there would move the failure from
a missing menu item to a wrong answer.

